 BINDING = [
-    {'what': "HUD edge anchor, v14 (hud_edge.c: entry + 0x13c cuts, compass 'PicStrap', lives 'Life'/'TxtLife', coins 'TxtCounterSh'/'TxtCounter', regional coins 'PicIconSh'/'PicIcon'/'TxtTotalShine' under a 'Counter', moons 'Counter'/'TxtTotalShine', hints 'TxtGuide01', matched by pane name only; the auto edge offset from the screen aspect -- iPhone 19.5:9 +140 out, iPhone Duo 1.43:1 -126 in, iPad 4:3 -160 in, 16:9 0 -- plus the launcher's manual settings from the DM_HUD_* environment variables (hud_manual.c, state page +0x200), which are a delta from the auto edge anchor (0128: the editor shows the element at its edge-anchored default and records the drag from there, so the manual offset is ADDED to the edge -- dragging in the editor moves the element by the same amount in the game, and a manual element still follows the aspect), and a hide that pushes the pane off-screen; the compass takes an extra +128 on its edge anchor (0128: its dial is centred in the 340-wide 'PicStrap' strip, so the plain edge puts the strip at the screen edge but the dial ~128 short of it -- the extra brings the dial, and the hints text in the strip, to the edge); a dirty flag so a moved container carries its children, an orig/mod table with the applied transform so a fixed offset never drifts, sixteen slots per HUD element (0126: log-20 shows TEN panes matching coins and eight slots thrashed, so the numbers drifted off-screen in V1.3.16); no settings UI in the game itself; 0123 regroups the moon icon + 020 into the coins element, splits the '+ menu / - map' hints into their own element, and adds parent compensation so a matched child of a matched parent (moon icon under the moons Counter, hints under the compass strip) is moved once, not twice; 0127 splits the two kinds of coins into two separately adjustable elements (coins, regional coins, moons), so the state page grows to 18 floats and the manual/hidden masks move to state +0x248/+0x24C; the white bar under the counts has no matching